{"Title":"An Act to inform prescribers of non-opioid alternative care","BillNumber":"S1254","DocketNumber":"SD637","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"EDJ0","Name":"Edward J. Kennedy","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/EDJ0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T10:16:32.933"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"EDJ0","Name":"Edward J. Kennedy","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/EDJ0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T10:16:32.9333333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1254/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Kennedy, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1254) of Edward J. Kennedy for legislation to inform prescribers of non-opioid alternative care.  Mental Health, Substance Use and Recovery.","DocumentText":"\tChapter 94C Sec 18 (e) of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting at the end thereof the following:  The Boards shall consult with Massachusetts Chiropractic Society during the process of developing the training programs, in order to insure that those programs include education for the prescribers that includes accurate information about chiropractic as an alternative form of care instead of opioids. \r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J18","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J18"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}